; ====================================================================================================
; THE ARENA (36D, rebuilt 37F) — where the Iron King is fought.
;
; ⚠️ WHAT IT WAS: a 36 m flat-grey BoxMesh floor, THREE BoxMesh walls (there was no west one), and a
; single CYLINDER brazier. The one arena_wall model per side was stretched 4.3x to span 36 m, which
; stretched its stonework with it. It read as a grey box because it was one.
;
; ⚠️ THE FIGHTING CIRCLE STAYS BARE, AND THAT RULE SURVIVED THE REBUILD INTACT. Everything added here
; is on the RIM or beyond it. A combat floor has to stay legible: scenery a player reads as cover, or
; that an add appears to path around, is worse than a bare floor. The ground cover at the bottom of
; this file is dress_cell.py's "edges" style for the same reason, and must stay that way.
;
; ⚠️ THE WEST SIDE USED TO BE OPEN "ON PURPOSE" AND IT WAS A BUG (the 2026-08-28 layout rebuild). The paragraph this
; replaces said the entrance was the west side at x = -18, with the challenge brazier at x = -14 and
; the player walking in past it. There is nothing west of this cell. The road into the arena comes
; from wilds_north at world (0, -142), which is this cell's local (0, 18) — the SOUTH edge — and
; EmberCrown.tres has drawn Path_arena_gate from exactly there since 38F. A full-width 36 m collider
; stood across it. The arena's door faced the void and its road faced a wall.
;
; THE ARENA NOW:
;   the gate       a 7.2 m gap in the SOUTH wall at x -3.6..3.6, flanked by the two gate pillars. The
;                  challenge brazier stands at (0, 13) just inside it, which is the first thing the
;                  player meets. Its Summon offset moved with it (see the Brazier block) so the king
;                  still rises at (0, 0, 0).
;   the west wall  now exists, as three stonework segments plus a collider. It closes the ring.
;   THE BREACH     x 6..12 in the NORTH wall, collapsed, with three rubble piles in and around it.
;                  It is the arena's asymmetry, its second way out, and the one place the ring is not
;                  a shape you can predict from any other part of it.
;   the stands     deliberately UNEVEN. Six tiers packed along the east, a broken run of four across
;                  the north-west, two on the west, none on the south — a crowd sits where it can see,
;                  not in four matched blocks at the compass points, which is what was here before.
;   the shrine     Drakar and his two spectators moved OFF the centre line to the north-west corner
;                  at (-14, -13), where they watch the floor instead of standing on the approach.
;
; ⚠️ THE FIGHTING CIRCLE STAYS BARE, AND THAT RULE SURVIVED THIS REBUILD TOO. Nothing added or moved
; here is inside 12 m of the centre. A combat floor has to stay legible: scenery a player reads as
; cover, or that an add appears to path around, is worse than a bare floor.
;
; ⚠️ FOUR NODE GROUPS ARE LOAD-BEARING AND MUST NOT BE RENAMED OR REPARENTED:
;   Brazier/Summon      BossSummonComponent — spawns the king at the brazier's +14 X offset
;   AddSpawns/Spawn*    found by GROUP "boss_add_spawn", so a rename unbinds nothing, but a MOVE
;                       drops an add on the boss or inside a wall
;   EmberVents/VentA-D  hidden OmniLights the phase hooks reveal
;   Phase2Hook/3Hook    their Reveals arrays are NodePaths to those vents — renaming a vent breaks
;                       the boss's phase telegraph SILENTLY, and nothing logs it
; ====================================================================================================

